{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MOD=1000000007;\nint q[65],k;\nlong long n;\nstruct Mat{\n\tint a[32][32];\n\tMat(){memset(a,0,sizeof(a));}\n\tMat operator*(const Mat&b)const{\n\t\tMat c;\n\t\tfor(int i=0;i<=k;++i)\n\t\t\tfor(int j=0;j<=k;++j)\n\t\t\t\tfor(int l=0;l<=k;++l)\n\t\t\t\t\tc.a[i][l]=(c.a[i][l]+1LL*a[i][j]*b.a[j][l])%MOD;\n\t\treturn c;\n\t}\n};\nMat pre[32],suf[32],f[65][32],ans;\nint main(){\n\tscanf(\"%lld%d\",&n,&k);\n\tans.a[0][k]=1;\n\tint cnt=0;\n\twhile(n){ q[++cnt]=n%k; n/=k; }\n\tfor(int i=0;i<k;++i)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<=k;++j)\n\t\t\tf[1][i].a[j][i]=f[1][i].a[j][j]=1;\n\tfor(int i=2;i<=cnt;++i){\n\t\tpre[0]=f[i-1][0];\n\t\tsuf[k-1]=f[i-1][k-1];\n\t\tfor(int j=1;j<k;++j) pre[j]=pre[j-1]*f[i-1][j];\n\t\tfor(int j=k-2;j>=0;--j) suf[j]=f[i-1][j]*suf[j+1];\n\t\tf[i][0]=suf[0];\n\t\tfor(int j=1;j<k;++j) f[i][j]=suf[j]*pre[j-1];\n\t}\n\tint sum=0;\n\tfor(int i=cnt;i>=1;--i){\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<q[i];++j)\n\t\t\tans=ans*f[i][(sum+j)%k];\n\t\tsum=(sum+q[i])%MOD;\n\t}\n\tint res=0;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<=k;++i) res=(res+1LL*ans.a[0][i])%MOD;\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\",res);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B, m):\n    \"\"\"Multiply two m x m matrices modulo MOD.\"\"\"\n    C = [[0] * m for _ in range(m)]\n    for i in range(m):\n        Ai = A[i]\n        Ci = C[i]\n        for j in range(m):\n            aij = Ai[j]\n            if aij:\n                Bj = B[j]\n                for l in range(m):\n                    Ci[l] = (Ci[l] + aij * Bj[l]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    m = k + 1  # matrix dimension\n\n    # compute digits of n in base k (least significant first)\n    digits = []\n    temp = n\n    while temp > 0:\n        digits.append(temp % k)\n        temp //= k\n    cnt = len(digits)\n\n    # f[i][j] for i from 1 to cnt, j from 0 to k-1\n    f = [None] * (cnt + 1)  # index 0 unused\n\n    if cnt >= 1:\n        # initialize f[1][j]\n        f[1] = [None] * k\n        for j in range(k):\n            mat = [[0] * m for _ in range(m)]\n            for row in range(m):\n                mat[row][row] = 1\n                mat[row][j] = 1\n            f[1][j] = mat\n\n        # build f[i] for i = 2..cnt\n        for i in range(2, cnt + 1):\n            pre = [None] * k\n            suf = [None] * k\n            pre[0] = f[i-1][0]\n            suf[k-1] = f[i-1][k-1]\n            for j in range(1, k):\n                pre[j] = mat_mul(pre[j-1], f[i-1][j], m)\n            for j in range(k-2, -1, -1):\n                suf[j] = mat_mul(f[i-1][j], suf[j+1], m)\n            f[i] = [None] * k\n            f[i][0] = suf[0]\n            for j in range(1, k):\n                f[i][j] = mat_mul(suf[j], pre[j-1], m)\n\n    # initialize ans matrix: ans[0][k] = 1\n    ans = [[0] * m for _ in range(m)]\n    ans[0][k] = 1\n\n    total = 0\n    # process digits from most significant to least\n    for idx in range(cnt-1, -1, -1):\n        digit = digits[idx]\n        i = idx + 1  # corresponding f index\n        for j in range(digit):\n            ans = mat_mul(ans, f[i][(total + j) % k], m)\n        total = (total + digit) % MOD\n\n    res = sum(ans[0][i] for i in range(m)) % MOD\n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.60526381782256e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0002703301142901182, -0.48977988958358765, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0009145130170509219, -0.008615466766059399, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -5.125986263010418e-06, -2.861018856492592e-06, -0.0009048658539541066, -1.883488948806189e-05, 0.0, -1.7046782886609435e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -9.667406266089529e-05, -0.006543045397847891, -4.708655978902243e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.7947855591773987, -0.03185548633337021, -0.0002324311062693596, -0.023374253883957863, -0.0002760506176855415, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.019683275371789932, 0.0, -0.006329253315925598, 0.0, -5.328513361746445e-05, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, -0.07890517264604568, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.5774968862533569, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1444026313256472e-05, 0.0, -0.061982180923223495, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -1.6689160474925302e-05, 0.0, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.5782467722892761, -0.0001070442158379592, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.291525328881107e-06, -0.18094965815544128, -0.0018373527564108372, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.0531076592742465e-06, 0.0, -0.000108951353468